# Shell scripts are executed inside Linux containers, so they must be checked out with LF
# whatever the host does.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the default on Windows here, and with no rule it rewrote
# `web/docker-entrypoint.d/40-runtime-config.sh` to CRLF on checkout. The kernel then looks for
# an interpreter named `/bin/sh\r`, nginx's entrypoint reports "not found", and the web container
# restart-loops with exit 127 - while `git status` stays clean, because the index holds LF and the
# conversion is exactly what autocrlf is supposed to do. Cost a rebuilt stack to find (2026-09-03).
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.envsh text eol=lf

# Same reason: read by the container's shell, not by a Windows editor.
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.template      text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
